WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.794
Hi! A whale lives in the sea, but is it a fish? A bat can fly, but is it a bird? Today we'll learn how to group animals.

2
00:00:10.944 --> 00:00:17.778
Mammals have hair or fur, and their young drink their mother's milk, like cats, dogs and people.

3
00:00:17.928 --> 00:00:21.618
Birds have feathers and a beak, and they lay eggs.

4
00:00:21.768 --> 00:00:26.010
Fish have scales and fins, and breathe in water with gills.

5
00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:33.978
An insect's body has three parts, head, thorax and abdomen, and it has 6 legs.

6
00:00:34.128 --> 00:00:39.402
Amphibians have moist skin and can live in water and on land, like frogs.

7
00:00:39.552 --> 00:00:45.042
Reptiles have dry, scaly skin, like lizards, snakes and crocodiles.

8
00:00:45.192 --> 00:00:49.458
Whales and bats both feed their young on milk, so they're mammals.

9
00:00:49.608 --> 00:00:55.674
Penguins can't fly, but they have feathers and a beak, so they're birds.

10
00:00:55.824 --> 00:01:01.578
Watch out! Many pupils think spiders are insects. That's wrong!

11
00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:08.898
Insects have 6 legs and three body parts. Spiders have 8 legs and only two body parts.

12
00:01:09.048 --> 00:01:15.570
So a spider is not an insect. Count the legs when you group animals.

13
00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:24.378
Your turn! Which group does a butterfly belong to? Pause and think.

14
00:01:24.528 --> 00:01:32.490
A butterfly has 6 legs and three body parts. It's an insect. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:41.130
Another one! Which group does a whale belong to? Pause and think.

16
00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:47.730
Baby whales drink milk, so whales are mammals. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:56.442
Here's another! Which group does a frog belong to? Pause and think.

18
00:01:56.592 --> 00:02:04.842
A frog has moist skin and lives in water and on land. It's an amphibian. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:04.992 --> 00:02:13.626
Try one more! Which group does a snake belong to? Pause and think.

20
00:02:13.776 --> 00:02:20.874
A snake has dry, scaly skin. It's a reptile. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:21.024 --> 00:02:30.546
Try one more! Is a spider an insect? Count its legs. Pause and think.

22
00:02:30.696 --> 00:02:40.506
A spider has 8 legs and 2 body parts, so it is not an insect. Insects have 6 legs. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:40.656 --> 00:02:48.594
Last one! What do fish use to breathe? Pause and think.

24
00:02:48.744 --> 00:02:55.410
Fish use their gills to take in oxygen from the water. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:55.560 --> 00:03:08.250
Remember: mammals have fur and feed on milk, birds have feathers, fish breathe with gills, insects have 6 legs, amphibians have moist skin, and reptiles have dry, scaly skin.

26
00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:14.586
Next time you visit the zoo, say which group each animal belongs to!

